{
  "title": "Blog fallback keeps a bold recipe title at the top of the first ingredient list as an ingredient",
  "description": "Some unstructured blog posts repeat the recipe title in bold as the first line of the first ingredient `<p>` (e.g. `<p><b>Blueberry Lavender Muffins</b><br>2 cups flour…`). extract_ingredient_lines_from_chunk (ramekin-core/src/extract/blog.rs) keeps that line as an ingredient. \
It only promotes a leading bold line to a section when detect_section_header accepts it as written, or when it opens a later ingredient list. \
Promoting any Title-Case bold line at the top of the first list would also swallow a bold ingredient like 'Fresh Parsley' (Codex review on #777). \
In data/unique-ingredients.txt this shows up as 'Bakery-Style Buttermilk Blueberry Muffins', 'Blueberry Lavender Muffins', 'Buttermilk Coconut Waffles', 'Coconut Chocolate Chip Cookies', 'Crispy Salted Peanut Butter Cookies', 'Nutella Raspberries Cupcakes' and 'Blueberries and Cream Bread Pudding'. \
Likely fix: drop the line when it matches the extracted recipe title (or page title) after normalization. \
Expect intentional data/ diffs from make pipeline: those recipes lose one ingredient line.",
  "status": "open",
  "priority": 4,
  "type": "bug",
  "labels": [
    "ingredient-parser",
    "pipeline",
  ],
